# Build context exclusions.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, and the production deploy rsyncs onto the server and builds
# there — so the build context is the *deploy directory*, not a clean checkout. Anything left
# lying around on the server gets baked into the image, even files that are not in git. That is
# how 9.2 MB of generated `graphify-out/` cache ended up inside the production image after it had
# already been removed from the repository.
#
# Each entry below is here because it was measured, not on principle. Paths starting with `/` are
# anchored to the context root, so a same-named directory deeper in the tree is untouched — in
# particular `app/data/` (which holds `anno_db_categories.json`, read at runtime) is NOT affected
# by the `/anno_db/` rule.

# ── Secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Untracked but present in a local checkout: a `docker build` here would bake it into the image.
# Production passes configuration through the environment, never through a file in the image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Generated caches (measured: 121 MB + 9.2 MB locally) ────────────────────
/graphify-out/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# ── Version control and tooling (measured: 19 MB) ───────────────────────────
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/
.superpowers/

# ── Virtualenvs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ── Test fixtures (measured: 73 MB, no reference anywhere in app/ or tests/) ─
# `tests/` itself is deliberately kept: it is only 1.8 MB and `make test` runs pytest inside the
# container.
/data_test/

# ── Annotation database (measured: 294 MB in the image, always dead weight) ─
# Only the r-worker uses it, and it is bind-mounted read-only from the host
# (`${ANNO_DB_HOST_PATH:-./anno_db}:/app/anno_db:ro`), so the copy inside the image is shadowed at
# runtime and never read. See the comment at `app/worker/tasks.py` on the r-worker mount.
/anno_db/

# ── Runtime storage (a volume mount target, never image content) ────────────
/data/

# ── Editor / OS noise ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# ── Local compose overrides and backups ─────────────────────────────────────
docker-compose.override.yml
*.bak
*.log
